.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tomat-daemon 1  "daemon " 
.SH NAME
daemon \- Manage the background daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdaemon\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the tomat daemon, which runs in the background and maintains timer state. The daemon must be running for timer commands to work.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tomat\-daemon\-start(1)
Start the daemon in the background
.TP
tomat\-daemon\-stop(1)
Stop the running daemon
.TP
tomat\-daemon\-status(1)
Check daemon status
.TP
tomat\-daemon\-install(1)
Install systemd user service
.TP
tomat\-daemon\-uninstall(1)
Uninstall systemd user service
.TP
tomat\-daemon\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
